  "prefLabel": "Auc 103.03 Functions of the Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Auc 103.03 Functions of the Board. The board shall, with the approval of the executive director of the OPLC, adopt rules for:\n\n(a) Establishing eligibility for certificates of authorization;\n\n(b) Establishing requirements for continuing education;\n\n(c) Determining how disciplinary actions by the board shall be implemented;\n\n(d) Establishing the qualifications of applicants for initial, renewal, and reinstatement licensure;\n\n(e) Determining how applicants demonstrate good professional character;\n\n(f) The required ethical and professional standards for licensees; and\n\n(g) Any other matters related to the proper administration of RSA 311‑B.\n\nSource. #6657, eff 1-1-98; ss by #12155, eff 4-5-17; ss by #14500, eff 2-8-26 (formerly Auc 103.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/auc100-500.html"
